Hi,

Here's the summary of today's IRC meeting.

---

COMMUNITY MEETING

Place: #openvpn-meeting on irc.freenode.net
Date: Monday 7th November 2016
Time: 20:00 CET (19:00 UTC)

Planned meeting topics for this meeting were here:

<https://community.openvpn.net/openvpn/wiki/Topics-2016-11-07>

The next meeting has not been scheduled yet.

Your local meeting time is easy to check from services such as

<http://www.timeanddate.com/worldclock>

SUMMARY

agi, cron2, dazo, lev, mattock and syzzer participated in this meeting.

---

Discussed patchwork:

<http://jk.ozlabs.org/projects/patchwork/>

It was agreed that even the minimal level ("show status of patches on=20
the list") would be useful, especially with community LDAP integration.=20
At a later point we can implement a more elaborate process such as this:

Patch comes in to openvpn-devel
Patchwork picks it up
Test "git apply"
   - Failure -> auto-reject
   - Success -> queue
Preliminary human review ("feature-ACK")
   - Makes sense -> trigger build test
     - Failure -> auto-reject
     - Success -> code review
   - Does not make sense -> reject

This approach would be DoS/misuse-resistant: starting builds=20
automatically from random patches sent to list would be dangerous on=20
many levels.

Mattock will start by setting up patchwork with the minimal feature set,=20
as discussed above.

---

Discussed basic Windows testing, which could be fully automated by=20
integrating these two tools together:

<https://github.com/mattock/openvpn-windows-buildtest>
<https://github.com/mattock/openvpn-windows-test>

The glue would probably more Powershell scripting, along with a=20
Chocolatey repository for OpenVPN:

<https://chocolatey.org/>

Wpkg was also mentioned as an option for Chocolatey, but it is less well=20
suited for a public-facing repository, as some of its features depend on=20
SMB shares.

---

Discussed OpenVPN 2.4 release schedule. It was agreed to set the=20
deadline for 2.4_beta1 to November 16th. That will give us some time to=20
finish the final set of really important patches. Any major features=20
that remain will be postponed for 2.5. The release date for 2.5_alpha1=20
could be set to ~6 months after 2.4.0, so this postponement of features=20
would not be the end of the work.

---

Discussed the only known openvpnserv2 issue:

<https://github.com/xkjyeah/openvpnserv2/issues/10>

Agreed that, if possible, the fix should go in to 2.4.0, but if=20
necessary, to a later point release. The fix is important, as it is=20
possible, in certain cases, for connectivity to break, if openvpnserv2=20
restarts a connection.

---

Discussed our systemd unit files, which would be good to have in all=20
distros; right now all distros have rolled up their own.  Our unit files=20
handle clients and servers separately, which has the benefit that it=20
allows seamless migrations, as well as fixes some issues with certain=20
Cloud providers:

<https://community.openvpn.net/openvpn/ticket/462>
<https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/openvpn/+bug/1580356>

Agi, the Debian package maintainer, will test our systemd unit files and=20
report back.

---

Discussed latest results from Coverity Scan. Our defect average is way=20
below industry average. The new "defects" in our current code (as=20
reported by Coverity) are not really defects, but more related to coding=20
style.

---

Discussed OpenVPN 2.3.14 release. The biggest thing missing is=20
"block-outside-dns v2". The remaining things are fairly minor in=20
comparison. Decided to release 2.3.14 after 2.4_beta1 is out to keep our=20
focus clear.

--=20

Full chatlog has been attached to this email.

--=20
